A||||13||BBBAD GT||First Impressions on New Fiero||||1||
Z||000000||BBBAD GT||02-07-2000||02:27 PM||||<BR>Picked up my 87 GT 5 speed last Saturday, and here are my first impressions:<P>1.  The shifter handle almost hits the sunroof (hehe).  I can't believe its that high, maybe I have a one off, but it actually on the same level as my shoulder.  I have to get a new shifter, anybody recommend one?  Are all the 'short shifters' on the market for the Fiero just shorten stock handles?<P>2.  The brakes feel spongy.  Sometimes it feels like I have to keep pushing on them to get the car to stop quicker.  Master cylinder problems?  Is this common?<P>3.  For a 13 yr old car with 85k miles, this car sure surprised me on how 'solid' it was.  No creaks or squeeks on the 3 hour drive back home.  The doors are alot heavier than I anticipated, but ok.  I'll just have to get used to the manual steering, but thats ok also.<P>4.  The emergency parking brake sure has an annoying buzzer, I'm sure everyone agrees on that one.<P>All in all, I'm happy with her so far.  It sure gets the looks, and that was part of the reason I purchased it.  Now, I just have to get use to the mid-engine handleing....(the fun part).....<P> <A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/</A> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||fiero56||02-07-2000||02:45 PM||||When I first got my Fiero, the parking brake buzzer was the first thing to go. I retained all the other buzzez, but no more parking brake buzzer. To do it, under the dash passenger side by the dingy thingy, is a brown wire with white stripe, cut it. Thats all there is, no more annoying p. brake buzzer. I actually wired in a flipper switch, and stuck it underneath the carpet in case the occasion should arise that I need it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||overlord||02-07-2000||05:13 PM||||my parking brake doesnt have a buzzer..<BR>its more of a "bing bing bing"<P>thank god it only comes on when it wants to.lol||||reg||1
Z||000003||87 Steve GT||02-07-2000||05:51 PM||||Bing.... bing....  mine too...  lol   Under the passenger side, under the dash. there is a BLUE square box (half the size of a deck of card's)... just pull it out, like you would pull out a fuse...   no more bing bing...lol...                Steve..||||reg||7
Z||000004||Monkeyman||02-07-2000||08:13 PM||||BBBAD GT--Went to your site. Didn't see any pics of your new Fiero.  Post some, please.||||reg||1
Z||000005||fiero56||02-07-2000||09:00 PM||||The blue dingy thingy also makes a great chew toy for the dog. Try it, they'll love you for it.<BR>I haven't heard the ding for the parking brake in a year, guess I should turn it on and see how long it takes to make me consider throwing it away. <BR>If your brakes are spongy, bleed all 4 before you do anything drastic. Start with the farthest from the m.c.(pass rear, then driver rear, pass front, driver front) and see if that solves the problem. Bleeder screws are 10mm.||||reg||1
Z||000006||BBBAD GT||02-07-2000||10:21 PM||||Thanks for the tip on the brakes.  I guess the spongy feel isn't a common feature (I'm still learning the GM thing).  Here are a couple pics of the GT.  Haven't had time to make a page for it, but will soon.<P>   <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/fiero1.jpg">   <P>  <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/fiero2.jpg">  <P><BR> [URL=My Web Site]http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/[/URL] <P>[This message has been edited by BBBAD GT (edited 02-07-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by BBBAD GT (edited 02-07-2000).]||||reg||6
