Z||000010||BBBAD GT||02-08-2000||10:17 AM||||I got a great deal on my Fiero, it has 85k miles and looks real good.  It does look like a 85k car on the inside, but that can be fixed with a little TLC.  I paid 3.2k for it, mainly because it had a salvage title with it (barely hit in the front, but was totaled by the Insurance company), but Ed Parks did the resotoration on it back in 1996.  Its my new daily driver, and I'm happy with it so far.<P>Fireospeeder:  Where in IL are you from?  I'm from Southern IL and would like to meet other Fiero guys at maybe autocross events or Fiero events.  Anybody else from IL?<P> <A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50" TARGET=_blank>http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50</A> <P>||||reg||14
Z||000011||Bill Osmer||02-08-2000||10:52 AM||||BBBad GT -<BR>Welcome to Fieros!!! Great lookin' car! Good price, too.<P>I've got a silver '86 GT fastback, too, and LOVE it. During Spring, Summer & Fall, it's my daily driver. Now you got me thinking... when's Spring coming!?!?!?!||||reg||1
